private activation/dependency evidence and exactly-once binding qualify the
current own surface without treating companion receipts as authority.
Missing crypto retains ordinary activation but cannot qualify MATCH.

Proof on integrated sources: affected loader/SDK/plugin/integration suite,
whole real companion suite, renderer tsc and ESLint exit 0; actual production
Vite loader/SDK plus whole companion replay MATCH; scripts/check 21 checks ok.
Prior independent frozen artifact review: 234+120 cases, 83/83 mutants killed,
30342 input hashes verified. Those mutation results are prior evidence, not
fresh integrated execution. No full Desktop/native acceptance claimed.
Companion changes will publish separately through guarded review and CI.

No runner changes, native probes, containment release, install or restart.
Later runner must freshly re-admit identity/controller before each mutation.

